// EXPECT: [E012]
// The companion: when a wrap IS possible the full type range is still the answer, so nothing is
// proven. `x` is an unconstrained `u8`, so `x +% 200` ranges over [200, 455] in exact arithmetic —
// which leaves `u8` — and the wrapped result may be any `u8` at all, including values that violate
// `k < 100`. Refused, which is what keeps the precise case above from being a hole.
func sink(k u8 < 100) u8 { return k }
func probe(x u8) u8 { return sink(x +% 200) }
func main() u8 { return probe(5) }
